                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "238703536",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561197992160522",
                            "num_reviews": 547,
                            "playtime_forever": 1148,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 1146,
                            "playtime_at_review": 1148,
                            "last_played": 1793129858
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1] LOST PLANET 3 [/h1]\n\n[h3] Positives: [/h3]\n+ The most gorgeous graphics ever that stands the test of time\n+ Fantastic shadow and lighting effects\n+ Very good sounds\n+ Awesome music\n+ Nice voiceacting\n+ The storytelling\n+ Very cinematic\n+ A beautiful planet with artistic environments\n+ Exploration is rewarded\n+ Achievements\n+ Nice length (about 10-15 hours)\n+ At its best its very enganging and entertaining...\n\n[h3] Negatives: [/h3]\n- ...But at its worst its very frustrating and repetitive\n- Controls are a mixed bag, especially in fights and in the rig\n- Boss fights are mostly a pain in the ass\n- Weird hitboxes\n- You must do things to proceed that was never explained to you (see below)\n- You will get stuck in places because of this\n- A lot of going back and forth in the same locations\n- Some side quests are just downright lazy and unfun\n- A few of the weapons are just make-weight\n- Bugs and glitches\n- Low FOV and 62 FPS lock out of the box (fixes for both below)\n\n[h3] Conclusion: [/h3]\nLost Planet 3 is like a interactive blockbuster movie that almost stumbles in its own execution.\nSure, there is a lot to like here: Especially the awesome graphics, music, voiceacting and storytelling.\nBut some parts are so frustrating, so poorly executed and unfun, that it hurts the overall experience.\nIts almost like the developer felt the game was too short, so they artificially extended it.\nAnd that never works in practice, when it does not move the story forward.\nSide quests are a good example of this, where you need to look for ten almost invisible creatures scattered across the entire map.\nIt takes a lot of time and gets frustrating because you dont know exactly where they are. And most of all, its boring as h*ll.\nAnd dont get me started on some of the controls, where you must understand things yourself that is never fully explained.\nDoes this make the game unplayable and skippable for some? Maybe.\nBut for most of us, if you can tolerate all the flaws, its a nice little diamond in the rough.\n\n[h1] Total Score: 7/10 [/h1]\n\n\n[b] PS! Here are some fixes and tips: [/b]\n\n[b] 1. [/b] The 62 FPS lock fix\n- Go to the configuration files location (usually C:\\Users\\*Username*\\Documents\\My Games\\LostPlanetGame\\LostPlanetGame\\Config\\)\n- Open the file LostPlanetEngine.ini\n- Search for and change two instances of bSmoothFrameRate to FALSE and raise two instances of MinSmoothedFrameRate, MaxSmoothedFrameRate and MinDesiredFrameRate to values of your liking (f.ex. 120).\n- Its very important to not set the FPS to anything higher than around 120, or else you can break some of the in-game control mechanics\n- Save the file and set it to read-only\n \n[b] 2. [/b] The low FOV fix\n- Go to the configuration files location (usually C:\\Users\\*Username*\\Documents\\My Games\\LostPlanetGame\\LostPlanetGame\\Config\\)\n- Open the file LostPlanetCamera.ini\n- To change FOV when on foot, change thirteen instances of DesiredFOV=75 with your FOV values (f.ex. 120)\n- To change FOV when using the utility rig, change two instances of DesiredFOV=85 with your FOV values (f.ex. 106)\n- You can also play around with the zoom FOV values if you like. But dont set them too high, or else you can break some of the in-game control mechanics (up to around 90 seems fine though)\n- Save the file and set it to read-only\n\n[b] 3. [/b] Download the free High-Res Movies DLC for better bitrate with much less compression artifacts\n\n[b] 4. [/b] When you get to use the claw arm on your rig, and must turn wheels, press F a lot of times instead of WASD to rotate it (if you cant, reduce the FPS to at least 120 or lower first)\n\n[b] 5. [/b] When you eventually encounter a scorpion monster while in the rig, do this:\nGrab its tail with mouse 1, and press and hold the W button to lift the monster's tail.\nIf you dont press W, the monster will spray and kill you fast.\nNow use mouse 2 to drill it.\nYou must do this procedure a few times till the tail eventually falls of.\n\n\n[i] Hopefully you are now all set, have fun out there! [/i]",
